# autoresearch-microapp-migration feedback log
# Append-only. Store stable preferences + loop lessons. Write incredibly tersely without but w/o sacrificing precision.

2026-03-19
- Use binary, verifiable checks only (CLI + API + screenshot/text), not subjective assessments.
- Always include explicit stop controls for autonomous loops (max loop count + deterministic stop reasons).
- Prioritize user-visible proof: command discoverability, command execution, state visibility, and screenshot signal.
- Enforce architecture boundaries during migration: microapps should use SDK seams, not direct core/window imports.
- If SDK surface changes, require docs sync in the same slice.
- Remember the COAT principle of WibWob-DOS: Command Once, Adapt Thin — no TUI-only semantics; features must remain API-visible.
- Scripts in this skill must be reusable across multiple microapps: parameterize command id, title regex, screenshot signal, and responsive mode field instead of hardcoding one app.
- Prefer `wibwob` CLI as the primary/faster control surface for live instance manipulation; use raw API calls as secondary verification.
- Use logical git commit parcels during long loops: commit verified milestones (migration complete, blocker fix, SDK+docs slice) and keep iterating.
- Also at end of migrations, invent 3 new microapps and autoresearch-loop them for UI quality and funness.
- Also at end of migrations,invent 3 new microapps and autoresearch loop them to enhance their UI and fun-ness
